From f07f240fd39e7eb3424c05b46983788553f83806 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Hawkins <phawkins@google.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:14:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [XLA:CPU] Reimplement Gloo reduce-scatter.

Gloo's built-in ReduceScatterHalvingDoubling has several data races that cause
data corruption on large buffers, and does not support timeouts. Replace its
use in GlooCommunicator with our own halving-doubling reduce-scatter
implementation that avoids the races and respects the collective timeout.

Issue https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/40830

PiperOrigin-RevId: 986074025
